  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In coil A, B $=\\frac{\\mu_0}{4 \\pi} \\frac{2 \\pi \\mathrm{I}}{\\mathrm{R}} . \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{B} \\alpha \\frac{\\mathrm{I}}{\\mathrm{R}}$; Hence, $\\frac{\\mathrm{B}_1}{\\mathrm{~B}_2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_1}{\\mathrm{R}_1} \\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{R}_2}{\\mathrm{I}_2}=\\frac{2}{2}=1$",
    "image": null
